  "body": "Migration M1 of the deployment-architecture epic (design: PR #5764 §7). Depends on the deploy tool v1.\n\nThe route proxy (`opencode-route-proxy.service`, :18750) is a hand-written unit file in `~/.config/systemd/user/` and is **broken today**: `activating/auto-restart`, `ExecMainStatus 127` — its `ExecStart` script (`~/code/bin/opencode-route-proxy-start.sh`) is not on disk, while a config comment already declared the proxy \"retired 2026-11-04 (opencode#1153)\". It is the canonical straddling-a-switch casualty.\n\nWork:\n- Define the route proxy as a services-layer target (package = the route-proxy from the opencode fork / deployed config source; health check = a real request through :18750).\n- Deploy it as the new generation; remove the hand unit file once the target is green.\n- Record the outcome on code#5610 — retiring or keeping the proxy becomes a target decision after this lands, not a switch edit.\n\nAcceptance: `deploy route-proxy status` shows two generations; :18750 serves through the new unit; a user-session restart does not resurrect the hand unit; `deploy route-proxy rollback` returns the previous generation and :18750 still serves.\n\nDo NOT retire the route proxy itself in this issue — #5610 owns that decision; this issue only moves its deployment mechanism.\n",
